# GCE VELA remote run (agent operator mode)

Invoke with `@gce-run`. **Agent runs terminal via Shell; never paste these commands for the user.**

**Goal:** Run VELA pipeline on `vst-vela-01` via `scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh`; read streamed output and local logs; iterate on failures.

**Judgment:** `.cursor/skills/gce-jupyter/SKILL.md` (browser Jupyter optional; terminal preferred for agent). **Cost:** `.cursor/skills/gce-ops/SKILL.md`.

| Name | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Project ID | `pt-vela` |
| VM | `vst-vela-01` |
| Zone | `europe-west4-a` |
| Bucket | `pt-vela-gce` |

---

## Cost gate

Before work: `@gce-start` or `scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh start`.

After success or failure: `@gce-stop` (always, unless user keeps VM running).

---

## Agent workflow (default)

From repo root on **Mac**:

```sh
chmod +x scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh start
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh status
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh run-resume   # if dataset + calibration already done
# or step by step:
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh run preflight
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh run pins
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh run export    # 10-20 min; use long shell timeout
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh run vela
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh run size
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh run upload
```

**Logs:**

- Stream: agent terminal (tee)
- VM: `~/vst/logs/agent_run.log`
- Mac: `scripts/gce_vela/outputs/<timestamp>/remote.log`

After a failure:

```sh
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh tail 120
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh pull-log
```

Fix `vm_run.py` or venv on VM, `remote.sh sync`, re-run failed step.

When pipeline finishes or session ends:

```sh
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh stop
scripts/gce_vela/remote.sh billing-status
```

---

## When user still wants Jupyter

Use `@gce-jupyter` (three terminals + Chrome). Terminal runner and Jupyter share the same `~/vst/.venv`.

